  "worked_solution": "The osculating plane passes through the point that is at the tip of the vector $r(0).$ The unit tangent vector $T(0)$ and the principal normal vector $N(0)$ are parallel to this plane. Therefore, a parametric equation for the plane can be written as \n\n$$\nR(s,u)=r(0)+sT(0)+uN(0),\\,s,\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\n \n\nWe have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0) & =\u27e8{e}^{0},\\,{e}^{0}\\operatorname{sin}\u20610,\\,{e}^{0}\\operatorname{cos}\u20610\u27e9=\u27e81,\\,0,\\,1\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, a parametric equation for the osculating plane at the point $(1,\\,0,\\,1)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s,u) & =r(0)+sT(0)+uN(0) \\\\  & =\u27e81,\\,0,\\,1\u27e9+s\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\u27e81,\\,1,\\,1\u27e9+u\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\u27e80,\\,1,\\,-1\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e81+\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{3}},\\,\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{3}}+\\frac{u}{\\sqrt{2}},\\,1+\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{3}}-\\frac{u}{\\sqrt{2}}\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
